  "goodToKnow": "Das Umland is the area surrounding a city: das Münchner Umland, Hamburg und Umland. As rents in big cities rise, many families move ins Umland and become Pendler (commuters). The affluent suburbs and commuter towns are jokingly called der Speckgürtel (bacon belt), especially around Berlin. Public transport in a city and its Umland is usually run by one Verkehrsverbund with shared tickets. It has no plural."
